A while loop will run a block of code as long as the condition is true. Here is the basic syntax for a while loop.

while (condition){
  //code block to be exexuted
}

The condition is checked before the blocl of the code is executed if the condition is false, the block of code will not be executed

While loops are useful whe you do not know how many times you need to run the block of code. here is an example of using awhile loop:

let counter = 0;
while(counter < 5) {
  console.log(counter);
  counter++;
}

In this example, we have avariable called counter that is initialized to 0. The while loop will continue to run as long as the value of counter is less than 5
inside the loop, we log the value couner to the console and then increment counter by 1.

Another loop similar to the while loop would be the do...while loop. Here is the Basic Syntax:
do{
  //code block to be executed
}while (condition);

Key different between a do...while loop and while loop is that the do...while loop will execute the block of code at least once before checking the condition.

If the condition is true the block od code will continue to execute. If the condition is false, the block of code will stop executing

Example1:(using do..while) loop

let counter = 0;
do {
  console.log(counter);
  counter++;
} while (counter < 5);  

In this example, we have a variable called counter that is initialized to 0. The do...while loop will log the value of the counter to the console and then increment
counter by 1. After executing the block if code, if checks if the value of counter is less than 5. if it is the loop will continue to run. If not, the loop will stop.

